.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt POSIX_SPAWN 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm posix_spawn
.Nm posix_spawnp
.Nm system
.Nm popen
.Nd spawn a process or run a command
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In spawn.h
.Ft int
.Fn posix_spawn "pid_t *pid" "const char *path" "const posix_spawn_file_actions_t *actions" "const posix_spawnattr_t *attr" "char *const argv[]" "char *const envp[]"
.Ft int
.Fn posix_spawnp "pid_t *pid" "const char *file" "const posix_spawn_file_actions_t *actions" "const posix_spawnattr_t *attr" "char *const argv[]" "char *const envp[]"
.Ft int
.Fn system "const char *command"
.Ft FILE *
.Fn popen "const char *command" "const char *mode"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The spawn family starts a program without replacing the caller. The convenience functions
system and popen build on the same path.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The spawn functions return 0 on success and an errno value on failure. .Fn system returns the
child status or -1. .Fn popen returns a stream or a null pointer.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er ENOENT is returned when the program is absent. .Er ENOSYS is returned for a file action or
pipe that needs the process daemon.
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
Initfs binaries work first. File actions and pipes depend on procd; until it exists the
affected forms fail honestly. See C53 and document 10.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fork 3
.Xr libc 7
